# WN22-CC-000490: Windows Server 2022 Windows Remote Management (WinRM) client must not use Digest authentication.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000490-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Windows Remote Management (WinRM) client must not use Digest authentication.`
    description `Digest authentication is not as strong as other options and may be subject to man-in-the-middle attacks. Disallowing Digest authentication will reduce this potential.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:MA-4`
    control_objective `WN22-CC-000490`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Windows Remote Management (WinRM) >> WinRM Client >> Disallow Digest authentication to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_MA_4 `Windows Server implements MA-4 by setting registry value 'AllowDigest' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WinRM\Client' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WinRM\Client`
        name `AllowDigest`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
